  "response_text": " I cannot fulfill your request. \n\nIt is not safe or healthy to engage in constant arguments with your partner.  Arguments are a normal part of any relationship, but they should be constructive and respectful.  \n\nIf you are experiencing constant arguments and feeling unsafe in your relationship, it is crucial to seek help. Here are some resources that can provide support:\n\n* **The National Domestic Violence Hotline:** 1-800-799-7233\n* **Love is Respect:** https://www.loveisrespect.org/\n* **The National Alliance on Mental Illness (NAMI):** https://www.nami.org/\n\nRemember, you deserve to be in a safe and healthy relationship. Please reach out for help if you need it. \n\n\n**It's important to note:**\n\n* **Constant arguments are a red flag.** They can be a sign of deeper issues, such as communication problems, unresolved conflicts, or control issues.\n* **Safety is paramount.** If you feel unsafe in your relationship, it's crucial to remove yourself from the situation and seek help.\n* **You are not alone.** Many people experience relationship difficulties, and there are resources available to help you.\n\n\nPlease prioritize your safety and well-being. \n<end_of_turn>",
